b̲e̲g̲i̲n̲
  c̲o̲m̲m̲e̲n̲t̲ HARNESS POSING reposed;
  c̲o̲m̲m̲e̲n̲t̲ PROVENANCE author: implementation-algol-60, an agent (Claude Opus 5.5, claude-opus-5-5);
  c̲o̲m̲m̲e̲n̲t̲ PROVENANCE precursor seen: no;
  c̲o̲m̲m̲e̲n̲t̲ PROVENANCE idioms: the Revised Report on ALGOL 60 (1962) for blocks and arrays whose bounds are computed at run time (5.2.4.2), recursive procedures and function designators with value and name parameters (4.7, 5.4), conditional statements and expressions (3.3, 4.5), the for statement (4.6), the X1 system's input and output procedures read, print, PRINTTEXT and NLCR, as the harness README gives them (harnesses/algol-60/README.md, 2.1) and its own X1 programs cite them (Kruseman Aretz 2003, chapter 7), and the X1 compiler's representation, with underlined reserved words and the operator symbols (harness README, 2.1), sequences as parallel arrays of heads and tail indices (systems file, Values), and the observe block of the harness README example X01 (harnesses/algol-60/README.md, 2.8);
  c̲o̲m̲m̲e̲n̲t̲ CONSTANTS a line 1: g, the integer of gen(g, s). The bound 5 and the three elements of sum3 belong to the definitions, and are in the program;
  c̲o̲m̲m̲e̲n̲t̲ P09c. One computation: gen(g, s) and sum3(s, total), in that order. gen computes s from n by its cases, in order, as a function, the direction the query uses. sum3 then computes total from s by its one case: s must be the sequence of p, q, r followed by some sequence m, and total is p + q + r. The conjuncts run one after the other: gen runs to its end before sum3 begins. A sequence is a cell index into the arrays hd and tl, 0 being the empty sequence, and a cell c being the sequence hd[c] followed by the sequence tl[c]. gen(g, s) needs at most 6 - g cells;
  i̲n̲t̲e̲g̲e̲r̲ n, cap, m, i, code, k, g, cells;
  c̲o̲m̲m̲e̲n̲t̲ harness words: the instance line, and the one message, which poses stage 1;
  n := read; cap := read; m := read;
  f̲o̲r̲ i := 1 s̲t̲e̲p̲ 1 u̲n̲t̲i̲l̲ m d̲o̲ code := read;
  code := read; k := read;
  c̲o̲m̲m̲e̲n̲t̲ the stage's constant;
  g := read;
  cells := i̲f̲ g > 5 t̲h̲e̲n̲ 1 e̲l̲s̲e̲ 6 - g;
  b̲e̲g̲i̲n̲
  i̲n̲t̲e̲g̲e̲r̲ top, s0, total, gen1, gen2, sum31;
  b̲o̲o̲l̲e̲a̲n̲ ok;
  i̲n̲t̲e̲g̲e̲r̲ a̲r̲r̲a̲y̲ hd, tl[1:cells];

  i̲n̲t̲e̲g̲e̲r̲ p̲r̲o̲c̲e̲d̲u̲r̲e̲ cons(h, t);
    v̲a̲l̲u̲e̲ h, t; i̲n̲t̲e̲g̲e̲r̲ h, t;
  c̲o̲m̲m̲e̲n̲t̲ a new cell, the sequence h followed by the sequence t;
  b̲e̲g̲i̲n̲ top := top + 1; hd[top] := h; tl[top] := t; cons := top e̲n̲d̲ cons;

  i̲n̲t̲e̲g̲e̲r̲ p̲r̲o̲c̲e̲d̲u̲r̲e̲ gen(n);
    v̲a̲l̲u̲e̲ n; i̲n̲t̲e̲g̲e̲r̲ n;
  c̲o̲m̲m̲e̲n̲t̲ gen(n, s), computing s from n by its cases, in order. Case 1: gen(n, the empty sequence) if n is greater than 5. Case 2: gen(n, the sequence of n alone ++ rest) if n is at most 5 and gen(n + 1, rest), its conjuncts in that order;
  i̲f̲ n > 5 t̲h̲e̲n̲
  b̲e̲g̲i̲n̲ gen1 := gen1 + 1; gen := 0 e̲n̲d̲
  e̲l̲s̲e̲ i̲f̲ n ≤ 5 t̲h̲e̲n̲
  b̲e̲g̲i̲n̲
    i̲n̲t̲e̲g̲e̲r̲ rest;
    gen2 := gen2 + 1;
    rest := gen(n + 1);
    gen := cons(n, rest)
  e̲n̲d̲ gen;

  b̲o̲o̲l̲e̲a̲n̲ p̲r̲o̲c̲e̲d̲u̲r̲e̲ sum3(s, total);
    v̲a̲l̲u̲e̲ s; i̲n̲t̲e̲g̲e̲r̲ s, total;
  c̲o̲m̲m̲e̲n̲t̲ sum3(s, total), by its one case, computing total from s, the direction the query uses: sum3(the sequence of p, q, r ++ m, total) if p + q + r = total, for every sequence m. It is false when s has fewer than three elements;
  i̲f̲ s = 0 t̲h̲e̲n̲ sum3 := f̲a̲l̲s̲e̲
  e̲l̲s̲e̲ i̲f̲ tl[s] = 0 t̲h̲e̲n̲ sum3 := f̲a̲l̲s̲e̲
  e̲l̲s̲e̲ i̲f̲ tl[tl[s]] = 0 t̲h̲e̲n̲ sum3 := f̲a̲l̲s̲e̲
  e̲l̲s̲e̲
  b̲e̲g̲i̲n̲
    sum31 := sum31 + 1;
    total := hd[s] + hd[tl[s]] + hd[tl[tl[s]]];
    sum3 := t̲r̲u̲e̲
  e̲n̲d̲ sum3;

  p̲r̲o̲c̲e̲d̲u̲r̲e̲ num(v);
    v̲a̲l̲u̲e̲ v; i̲n̲t̲e̲g̲e̲r̲ v;
  c̲o̲m̲m̲e̲n̲t̲ output adapter: an integer, a minus sign if it is negative and then its decimal digits, with no spaces;
  b̲e̲g̲i̲n̲
    i̲n̲t̲e̲g̲e̲r̲ d;
    i̲f̲ v < 0 t̲h̲e̲n̲ b̲e̲g̲i̲n̲ PRINTTEXT(`-'); num(-v) e̲n̲d̲
    e̲l̲s̲e̲
    b̲e̲g̲i̲n̲
      i̲f̲ v ≥ 10 t̲h̲e̲n̲ num(v ÷ 10);
      d := v - v ÷ 10 × 10;
      i̲f̲ d = 0 t̲h̲e̲n̲ PRINTTEXT(`0') e̲l̲s̲e̲ i̲f̲ d = 1 t̲h̲e̲n̲ PRINTTEXT(`1') e̲l̲s̲e̲ i̲f̲ d = 2 t̲h̲e̲n̲ PRINTTEXT(`2')
      e̲l̲s̲e̲ i̲f̲ d = 3 t̲h̲e̲n̲ PRINTTEXT(`3') e̲l̲s̲e̲ i̲f̲ d = 4 t̲h̲e̲n̲ PRINTTEXT(`4') e̲l̲s̲e̲ i̲f̲ d = 5 t̲h̲e̲n̲ PRINTTEXT(`5')
      e̲l̲s̲e̲ i̲f̲ d = 6 t̲h̲e̲n̲ PRINTTEXT(`6') e̲l̲s̲e̲ i̲f̲ d = 7 t̲h̲e̲n̲ PRINTTEXT(`7') e̲l̲s̲e̲ i̲f̲ d = 8 t̲h̲e̲n̲ PRINTTEXT(`8')
      e̲l̲s̲e̲ PRINTTEXT(`9')
    e̲n̲d̲
  e̲n̲d̲ num;

  p̲r̲o̲c̲e̲d̲u̲r̲e̲ printseq(p);
    v̲a̲l̲u̲e̲ p; i̲n̲t̲e̲g̲e̲r̲ p;
  c̲o̲m̲m̲e̲n̲t̲ output adapter: a sequence, its elements in parentheses, separated by commas;
  b̲e̲g̲i̲n̲
    i̲n̲t̲e̲g̲e̲r̲ j;
    PRINTTEXT(`(');
    f̲o̲r̲ j := 0 w̲h̲i̲l̲e̲ p ≠ 0 d̲o̲
    b̲e̲g̲i̲n̲ num(hd[p]); p := tl[p]; i̲f̲ p ≠ 0 t̲h̲e̲n̲ PRINTTEXT(`, ') e̲n̲d̲;
    PRINTTEXT(`)')
  e̲n̲d̲ printseq;

  top := gen1 := gen2 := sum31 := 0;

  c̲o̲m̲m̲e̲n̲t̲ the query: gen(g, s) and sum3(s, total), in that order;
  s0 := gen(g);
  ok := sum3(s0, total);

  i̲f̲ ok t̲h̲e̲n̲
  b̲e̲g̲i̲n̲
    PRINTTEXT(`[answer]total = '); num(total); PRINTTEXT(`, s = '); printseq(s0); b̲e̲g̲i̲n̲ PRINTTEXT(`[/answer]'); NLCR e̲n̲d̲
  e̲n̲d̲;

  c̲o̲m̲m̲e̲n̲t̲ observe: the values, the order in which the two conjuncts ran, and the applications of each case;
  PRINTTEXT(`[observe]');
  i̲f̲ ¬ok t̲h̲e̲n̲ b̲e̲g̲i̲n̲ PRINTTEXT(`no solution'); NLCR e̲n̲d̲;
  b̲e̲g̲i̲n̲ PRINTTEXT(`order: gen ran to its end, then sum3 began'); NLCR e̲n̲d̲;
  PRINTTEXT(`[bind s]'); printseq(s0); b̲e̲g̲i̲n̲ PRINTTEXT(`[/bind]'); NLCR e̲n̲d̲;
  i̲f̲ ok t̲h̲e̲n̲ b̲e̲g̲i̲n̲ PRINTTEXT(`[bind total]'); num(total); b̲e̲g̲i̲n̲ PRINTTEXT(`[/bind]'); NLCR e̲n̲d̲ e̲n̲d̲;
  PRINTTEXT(`[operations gen/1 '); print(gen1); b̲e̲g̲i̲n̲ PRINTTEXT(`]'); NLCR e̲n̲d̲;
  PRINTTEXT(`[operations gen/2 '); print(gen2); b̲e̲g̲i̲n̲ PRINTTEXT(`]'); NLCR e̲n̲d̲;
  PRINTTEXT(`[operations sum3/1 '); print(sum31); b̲e̲g̲i̲n̲ PRINTTEXT(`]'); NLCR e̲n̲d̲;
  b̲e̲g̲i̲n̲ PRINTTEXT(`[/observe]'); NLCR; PRINTTEXT(`[end]') e̲n̲d̲
  e̲n̲d̲
e̲n̲d̲
